From: retroforge
Subject: [PATCH] steamcompmgr: route second-screen windows to the secondary output

NDS/3DS emulators put their second screen in a second top-level window
of the same process: melonDS titled it "[w2] ...", Azahar ends it with
"| Secondary Window". Both are plain, non-transient toplevels carrying
the game's STEAM_GAME, so gamescope showed whichever mapped last on the
main panel (Azahar), or the one OpenGamepadUI named in
GAMESCOPECTRL_BASELAYER_WINDOW (melonDS): the DS bottom screen on the
top panel.

With --secondary-output, a window goes to the secondary output when its
GAMESCOPE_OUTPUT property is 1, or, without the property, when its
title matches the regex (ECMAScript, searched) in its Xwayland root
window's GAMESCOPE_SECONDARY_WINDOW_TITLE string property. Whoever
starts a dual-screen program sets that property before its windows map
(RetroForge's launcher, from the emulator's own definition) and every
window of that Xwayland is re-placed when it changes; empty or absent,
there is no title rule, and an invalid regex is logged and ignored.
gamescope knows no emulator's titles. Such a window is never a focus
candidate for the main output, which also keeps it out of
GAMESCOPE_FOCUSABLE_WINDOWS and out of a BASELAYER_WINDOW match, so the
main pick falls back to the game's other window. A separate secondary
focus picks the newest of them and sizes it to the panel (the panel's
orientation applied, as reported by IBackend::GetSecondaryOutputSize);
client resize requests on it are clamped to that size, and the desktop
window resize skips it. The secondary focus takes no part in focus
control: no appid, overlays or input focus.

Nothing is painted on the secondary output yet (next patch).

(retroforge: dual-screen boards, step 3 of the dual-output plan, 2026-10-12.
Window shapes read with xprop on the Thor Lite: melonDS 1.1 with
Window1 enabled, Azahar 2126.1.2 with layout_option=4. 2026-11-15: the
--secondary-window-title flag and its built-in melonDS/Azahar default
gave way to the root property when DSperate replaced melonDS.)
---
diff --git a/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp b/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp
index 9f9b760..780c3a9 100644
--- a/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp
+++ b/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp
@@ -1096,6 +1096,8 @@ static void setup_secondary_output( struct drm_t *drm )
 	if ( !pMode )
 		return fail( "no mode" );
 	sec.mode = *pMode;
+	// The panel's orientation property (a rotated panel reports which side is up).
+	sec.pConnector->UpdateEffectiveOrientation( &sec.mode );
 
 	if ( drmModeCreatePropertyBlob( drm->fd, &sec.mode, sizeof( sec.mode ), &sec.uModeBlobId ) != 0 )
 		return fail( "cannot create its mode blob" );
@@ -5137,6 +5139,19 @@ namespace gamescope
 			return &s_HeadlessConnector;
 		}
 
+		virtual bool GetSecondaryOutputSize( uint32_t *puWidth, uint32_t *puHeight ) override
+		{
+			const drm_secondary_t &sec = g_DRMSecondary;
+			if ( !sec.pConnector )
+				return false;
+
+			const GamescopePanelOrientation eOrientation = sec.pConnector->GetCurrentOrientation();
+			const bool bSideways = eOrientation == GAMESCOPE_PANEL_ORIENTATION_90 || eOrientation == GAMESCOPE_PANEL_ORIENTATION_270;
+			*puWidth = bSideways ? sec.mode.vdisplay : sec.mode.hdisplay;
+			*puHeight = bSideways ? sec.mode.hdisplay : sec.mode.vdisplay;
+			return true;
+		}
+
 		virtual IBackendConnector *GetConnector( GamescopeScreenType eScreenType ) override
 		{
 			if ( g_DRM.pConnector && g_DRM.pConnector->GetScreenType() == eScreenType )
